{"id": "EUVD-2026-108313", "enisaUuid": "cfaf1f2e-384f-3808-b70b-4c418379ad31", "description": "Wasmtime 46.0.0 before 48.0.4 and 49.0.0 before 49.0.2 contains a denial of service vulnerability in the wasmtime-wasi WASIp3 implementation that allows guests to abort the Unix host process. Guests with mutable preopened directory access can call set-times or set-times-at with negative seconds timestamps before the epoch, triggering an assertion failure that crashes the host.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:52", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-mr2v-56j5-cmfc", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wasmtime-46.0.0-before-48.0.4-and-49.0.0-before-49.0.2-host-panic-via-wasip3-timestamps"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c8j4-4v4r-vm84", "CVE-2026-115385"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ac90bfbf-bc7e-3a3b-8d67-aaa99979c961", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "49.0.0 <49.0.2"}, {"id": "bed7a4b6-8b10-3e40-a337-203bd36dee22", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "46.0.0 <48.0.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dca8258a-3971-3656-b764-6adab8adaa32", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}], "isExploited": false}